diff --git a/docs/inventory-screen.md b/docs/inventory-screen.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..881ba5b
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/inventory-screen.md
@@ -0,0 +1,82 @@
+# Inventory screen
+
+The inventory screen shows all ten block types and lets the player choose which one to build with.
+Code lives in `src/StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts/UI/`. `Main.client.luau` starts it by
+calling `InventoryUI.start()`.
+
+## What the player sees
+
+- **Blocks button** at the bottom centre of the screen, always visible while the screen is
+  closed. It shows a swatch of the block being built with, its name and how many are left
+  (`Brick x48`), and the shortcut for the current input (a `B` key cap, or the controller's Y
+  button). Bottom centre stays clear of the mobile thumbstick (bottom left) and jump button
+  (bottom right).
+- **Inventory screen**: a dimmed backdrop with a panel in the middle.
+  - Header: "My Blocks", the player's level (`Level 3`), and a large ✕ close button.
+  - Grid: one tile per block type, in hotbar order. Each tile has a colour swatch, the name, and
+    a count badge. Up to 5 columns; on small or portrait screens it uses fewer columns and
+    scrolls.
+  - Info bar: describes the tile in focus ("Brick: 48 blocks.", "🔒 Ice unlocks at level 4.
+    You're level 3.") and lists the buttons for the current input.
+- **Tile states**
+  - *Building with this*: thick gold outline and a gold ✓ badge.
+  - *Locked*: dark cover with a padlock, "Level N", and the name. The count is hidden. The
+    padlock and text mean it doesn't rely on colour alone.
+  - *None yet*: count shows a dimmed `0`. The tile can still be chosen, the same way the number
+    keys can choose it.
+  - *Focused* (mouse hover or controller selection): white outline, lighter fill, grows slightly.
+
+Tiles are at least 96×88 px, which is easy to hit with a thumb, and two rows fit on a landscape
+phone without scrolling. The panel stays inside the device safe area (notches and rounded
+corners); the backdrop covers the whole screen.
+
+## Opening and closing
+
+| | Touch | Mouse and keyboard | Controller |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Open | Tap the Blocks button | Click the Blocks button, or press **B** | Press **Y** |
+| Close | Tap ✕, or tap outside the panel | Click ✕, click outside the panel, or press **B** | Press **B** (or **Y**) |
+| Choose a block | Tap its tile (the screen closes) | Click its tile (the screen closes) | Move with the left stick or D-pad, press **A** (the screen closes) |
+| Locked block | Tap it: it shakes and the info bar says which level unlocks it | Hover to read the info bar; clicking shakes it | Select it to read the info bar; **A** shakes it |
+| Learn about a block | Tap a locked tile; unlocked tiles are chosen right away | Hover the tile | Select the tile |
+
+Notes on each input:
+
+- **Touch.** One tap chooses and closes, because most players are kids on phones and the usual
+  goal is "switch block and keep building". Hover never happens on touch, so the focus outline
+  isn't shown for taps and the info bar shows "Tap a block to build with it." until a locked
+  tile is tapped.
+- **Mouse and keyboard.** B toggles the screen, so the same key opens and closes it. Escape is
+  left alone because Roblox uses it for its own menu. The backdrop is a modal button, so the
+  cursor is freed from shift lock and first person while the screen is open. Number keys 1–0
+  still choose blocks (as before), and each unlocked tile shows its number key in the corner as a
+  reminder.
+- **Controller.** Opening puts the selection on the block being built with, so pressing A right
+  away keeps the current choice. Selection can't leave the panel. The ✕ button isn't selectable;
+  B closes instead, and the B and A button images in the info bar come from Roblox, so they match
+  Xbox or PlayStation controllers. If Roblox clears the selection while the screen is open, the
+  screen closes so it can't get stuck with nothing selected.
+
+Switching input mid-screen (say, from touch to a controller) updates the hints and moves or clears
+controller selection to match.
+
+## While the screen is open
+
+- Clicking or tapping places no blocks (`BlockPlacer.setEnabled(false)`); the previous setting
+  comes back on close.
+- The Blocks button is hidden.
+- Counts, locks and the level update live when `BlockInventory.Changed` fires, and the gold
+  outline follows `BlockPlacer.BlockTypeChanged`, so number keys pressed while the screen is open
+  show up straight away.
+
+## Files
+
+- `UI/InventoryUI.luau`: mounts the UI; open, close, toggle and choose; key and button bindings;
+  controller selection.
+- `UI/InventoryState.luau`: Vide sources for open state, input mode, selected block, focused tile
+  and inventory revision.
+- `UI/Components/InventoryButton.luau`: the Blocks button.
+- `UI/Components/InventoryScreen.luau`: backdrop, panel, header, grid and info bar.
+- `UI/Components/BlockTile.luau`: one tile.
+- `UI/Theme.luau`, `UI/Format.luau`: colours and sizes; count formatting and controller button
+  images.
